# PLANNING DIRECTIVE: GEO-VISOR ENGINE & EMITTER PIPELINE (v1.0.0-MVP)
Document Control: Core Product & Architectural Specification
Scope: Open-Source CLI, Deterministic Tool Compiler, & Multi-Format Emitter Engine

---

## 1. EXECUTIVE MANDATE & STRATEGIC OBJECTIVES

### 1.1 Core Mission
Build a lightweight, zero-LLM-overhead, single-binary CLI tool in Go (`geovisor`) that deterministically inspects active web pages (via Chromium DevTools Protocol), extracts human-centric UI elements (forms, navigation structures, dynamic interactive controls across Shadow DOM boundaries and frames), compiles them into a unified Tool Intermediate Representation (TIR), and emits strongly typed tool definitions across major agentic formats (WebMCP, Anthropic MCP static specs, and Universal OpenAI Function Calling).

### 1.2 Core Architectural Axioms
1. Zero LLM Dependency in Core Engine: The compilation process must be 100% deterministic, algorithmic, and local. Tool generation relies strictly on DOM introspection, event listener reflection, accessibility trees, Shadow DOM traversal, and non-LLM layout heuristics—not Vision LLM screenshots or token-heavy API calls.
2. Viewport & Context Isolation: Operate strictly on a per-page/active-viewport context across frames. Do not inline external assets or recursively crawl linked external domains into the active tool manifest. Unsupported media (e.g., PDFs) are indexed as static resource pointers with specialist tool hints.
3. Target Agnosticism via TIR: Never compile directly from DOM to a target output format. All raw DOM extractions are compiled into an internal Tool Intermediate Representation (TIR) before passing through targeted Emitters.
4. Scoped Locator Strategy: Standardize locator generation around scoped hierarchy bindings (`ContainerLocator >> ARIA Locator`) to survive single-page application (SPA) DOM re-renders and avoid strict-mode locator collisions in downstream agent runtimes.
5. Static Schema Emission: Operate as a pure static compiler/generator CLI (`visor inspect <url>`). Produce fully compliant static schema payloads (e.g., Anthropic MCP `tools/list` JSON, OpenAI function specs) without forcing the CLI to act as a long-running daemon server.

