## 8. DEFINITION OF DONE & SUCCESS METRICS

1. Compilation Speed SLA: In-memory Go TIR compilation and static format emission must complete in `< 50ms` after receiving CDP payload. Total execution time governed strictly by network load and `--timeout` flags.
2. Determinism: Identical DOM states across frames must produce 100% identical TIR and tool manifest structures across repeated executions.
3. Zero Token Footprint: Engine must output fully populated, strongly typed tool specifications without issuing external LLM or vision API calls.
4. Locator Resilience: 100% of generated locators must use scoped parent paths (`ContainerLocator >> ARIA Locator`) to prevent strictness violation collisions in agent runtimes.
5. DOM Boundary Coverage: Successfully extract form and input controls nested inside open Shadow DOM structures and cross-origin standard `<iframe>` contexts.
6. Standalone Portability: Binary compiles cleanly across macOS, Linux, and Windows with zero external runtime dependencies beyond an installed Chromium browser core.